So, your solution should include filtering out assert lines from the given C# code. You would use a simple string matching or a regular expression to identify and ignore lines starting with "@@@". 

Here is an example of filtering out the lines in C# using `String.StartsWith` and Regular expression:

```cs
using System;
using System.Text.RegularExpressions;

public class Program
{
    public static void Main()
    {
        string input = @"Some lines
Some assert lines @@@ should be ignored
Some more lines
More @@@ @@@ lines";

        var lines = input.Split(new[] { '\n' }, StringSplitOptions.None);
        foreach (var line in lines)
        {
            if (!Regex.IsMatch(line, @"^\s*\/\/\s*@@@", RegexOptions.IgnoreCase))
                Console.WriteLine(line);
        }
    }
}
```

